%I A401846 #14 Nov 14 2026 09:23:42
%S A401846 2,3,11,19,43,149,593,6197
%N A401846 a(n) is either the minimum of p(n) for p being an n-tuple of strictly increasing primes for which the set {p(i) + p(j) + p(k) : i < j < k} contains A111384(n) primes, or 0 if no such n-tuple exists.
%C A401846 A401846(n) = T401903(n,n) where T401903(n,k) is the triangle of the values of A401903.
%C A401846 a(9) is nonzero and a(9) <= 72937, see comments in A401903.
%H A401846 Markus Sigg, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.14840">A note on OEIS sequence A111384</a>, arXiv:2309.14840 [math.CO], 2023.
%H A401846 James Youlton, <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20240604035253/http://v-sonline.com/VSPCs/index.pl?C4">Virtual Source Programming Contests, Tribal Primes (Wayback Machine URL)</a>, 2009.
%Y A401846 Cf. A111384, A401903.
%K A401846 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A401846 1,1
